Verse 1:
[Eb]Let us break [Cm]bread to[Fm7]gether [Bb7]on our [Eb]kne[Ab]es,[Eb]
[Eb]Let us break bread to[Cm]gether [F]on our [Bb]kne[Cm]es.[Bb]
[Eb]When I fall [Bbm]on my [C]knees with [C7]my [Fm]face to the [Fm7]rising [Bb7]sun,
[Bb7]O[Eb]Lord, [Gm7]have [Ab]mercy [Bb7]on[Ab]me.[Eb]

Verse 2:
[Eb]Let [Cm]us [Fm7]drink [Bb7]wine [Eb]together [Ab]on [Eb]our knees,
[Eb]let [Cm]us [F]drink wine [Bb]together [Cm]on [Bb]our knees.
[Eb]When [Bbm]I fall [C]on my [C7]knees with [Fm]my face [Fm7]to the [Bb7]rising sun,
[Bb7][Eb]O [Gm7]Lord, [Ab]have [Bb7]mercy [Ab]on [Eb]me.

Verse 3:
[Eb]Let [Cm]us [Fm7]praise [Bb7]God [Eb]together [Ab]on [Eb]our knees,
[Eb]let [Cm]us [F]praise God [Bb]together [Cm]on [Bb]our knees.
[Eb]When [Bbm]I fall [C]on my [C7]knees with [Fm]my face [Fm7]to the [Bb7]rising sun,
[Bb7][Eb]O [Gm7]Lord, [Ab]have [Bb7]mercy [Ab]on [Eb]me.
